WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.625
The Patch Bay is the whole instrument as one hardware faceplate.

2
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:06.097
Maximize it to see more.

3
00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:12.377
Along the top, the Sources bus offers signals: waveforms, audio, beats, MIDI, and more.

4
00:00:12.377 --> 00:00:16.532
Every parameter has an input jack, a knob, and an output jack.

5
00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:19.377
Cables run from an output to an input.

6
00:00:19.377 --> 00:00:24.274
Drag the triangle wave toward the bottom edge, and the board scrolls with you.

7
00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:29.045
Drop it on Function Generator one, the same slot as in the Modulation panel.

8
00:00:29.506 --> 00:00:30.496
Now its output.

9
00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.666
Grab the output jack, and carry it up to H Size.

10
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.221
Restore the window.

11
00:00:35.221 --> 00:00:38.642
The raster now stretches in and out with the triangle wave.

12
00:00:39.101 --> 00:00:42.747
Back in the bay, grab a cable by its input end to move it.

13
00:00:42.747 --> 00:00:43.879
Drop it on V Size.

14
00:00:44.342 --> 00:00:46.710
Drop a cable in empty space to unplug it.

15
00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:51.138
Cables and the Modulation panel are two views of one patch.

16
00:00:51.138 --> 00:00:51.945
Next: nodes.
